instructions.en:
# Repair the Generated Test

The starter test was generated from a vague prompt. It uses a structural CSS locator, a fixed sleep, and a one-time `textContent` check. Repair it so that it:

1. locates `Submit order` by role and accessible name;
2. clicks once;
3. uses a web-first assertion to prove the status contains `Order submitted`;
4. contains no `waitForTimeout`.

Do not catch or suppress assertion errors.

instructions.id:
# Perbaiki Test Hasil Generate

Starter test dibuat dari prompt yang samar. Kode memakai structural CSS locator, fixed sleep, dan pemeriksaan `textContent` satu kali. Perbaiki agar:

1. menemukan `Submit order` berdasarkan role dan accessible name;
2. mengklik satu kali;
3. memakai web-first assertion untuk membuktikan status berisi `Order submitted`;
4. tidak memiliki `waitForTimeout`.

Jangan menangkap atau menyembunyikan assertion error.

challenges.starterCode:
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('submit order', async ({ page }) => {
  const button = page.locator('main > section.checkout-shell > button');
  await button.click();
  await page.waitForTimeout(1000);
  const message = await page.locator('p').textContent();
  expect(message).toBeTruthy();
});
